**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Resolve gateway effort in the session profile**

When a Gateway turn belongs to a named profile, `_run_gateway_chat_streaming` is running on a new thread with no request-profile TLS, so its preceding `cfg = get_config()` resolves the process/default profile rather than `s.profile`. These added lines now put that other profile's effort in authoritative `model_options` (and the legacy branch repeats it), causing named-profile chats to run with the default profile's reasoning setting; bind the config read to `s.profile` or pass a profile-owned snapshot into the worker.

