**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Resolve runner effort in the session profile**

For a `runner-local` process/delegation wakeup on a named-profile session, `start_session_turn` calls `_start_run` from the detached drain thread; the short profile scope in `_server_initiated_turn_routing` has already exited by the time this new `get_config()` executes. It consequently resolves the process/default profile and sends that profile's effort in a request that otherwise correctly names `s.profile`, so the explicit override can replace the runner's correct named-profile default; read the session's config under `profile_scope_for_detached_worker` or reuse a captured profile snapshot.

