<!-- lmstudio-snapshot-probe-2026-10-15:start -->
## Maintainer re-gate follow-up — LM Studio probe snapshot isolation (2026-10-15)

Addressed the final finding from the re-gate of `b044e2a91e3b` ([review #5523470304](https://github.com/nesquena/hermes-webui/pull/8241#pullrequestreview-5523470304)) in commit `3de670dcedbd2b9681b01a8de5f8eb16fdbb27a2`:

- Explicit LM Studio reasoning probes now resolve both the configured endpoint and API key from the request's lock-protected profile snapshot.
- Legacy callers that do not supply a snapshot retain their historical global-cache call shape.
- A two-thread regression pauses each request after explicit-provider selection, reloads the process-global cache to another profile, and proves both Gateway and runner lanes probe only the analyst endpoint/key and retain `high` instead of degrading to `low`.

Verification on the exact uploaded tree `6876150ca3f405900ce1050c2459e6e2df1fec0b`:

- Gateway/runner model-options boundary: **27 passed, 1 skipped**.
- Adjacent LM Studio/reasoning suites: **87 passed, 1 skipped**.
- Changed-test Ruff, Python compilation, and `git diff --check`: clean.
- Whole-file Ruff for `api/config.py` still reports its three pre-existing findings (unused `traceback`, unused `parse_qs`, duplicate `collections` import); none are in this diff.

Fresh exact-head CI and maintainer/review-bot re-gate remain pending.
